<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Debug and test runs only. The shipped app is sandboxed — see
         GalacticChessInvaders.entitlements, which Release uses.

         The sandbox is off here because CoreAudio's analytics client aborts
         under it rather than degrading: "Process is sandboxed but
         'com.apple.security.exception.mach-lookup.global-name' doesn't contain
         'com.apple.audioanalyticsd'". Under XCTest the host app is launched by
         the test runner and hits that on audio preload, so the whole suite dies
         before a single assertion runs.

         The alternative is a temporary-exception mach-lookup entitlement, which
         would then be carried into the shipped build and reviewed there. Not
         sandboxing a build that never leaves this machine is the smaller thing
         to be wrong about. -->
</dict>
</plist>
